  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nTuesday and Wednesday are shaping up to be a dry period following\nthe departure of the weather system and the setup of a zonal to\nsouthwest flow. Temperatures during this time will most likely see\na rebound back into the 70s to even low 80s.\n\nThen for Thursday into next weekend a large scale trough has\nbetter chances than not to deepen across western CONUS. This will\nallow for moisture to return across the panhandles while\nintroducing broad scale lift. As such the end of the week into the\nweekend will more likely be a period of wetter weather with rain\nshowers and thunderstorms.",
